,"heading":false},{"text":"“Ye didn’t say that up yonder,” said she.","heading":false},{"text":"Then she sprang to its side, and snatching it to her breast and bending o’er it a face, tender as th…","heading":false},{"text":"“I’ll think on it.”","heading":false}]},{"id":"7696831315902964313_63361-h-3.htm","href":"7696831315902964313_63361-h-3.htm.xhtml","linear":true,"types":[],"docTitle":"A RETROSPECT","navLabel":"A RETROSPECT","blocks":[{"text":"A RETROSPECT","heading":true},{"text":"A RETROSPECT","heading":false},{"text":"Martha laughed harshly.","heading":false},{"text":"The woman looked at him sharply.","heading":false},{"text":"He brought his slow gaze back to her.","heading":false},{"text":"Milly’s eyes shone and she clapped her hands.","heading":false},{"text":"“For me! What, niver!” she murmured.","heading":false},{"text":"But she talked for two.","heading":false},{"text":"“I shouldn’t wonder,” agreed Bill Hewson through his mufflers.","heading":false},{"text":"And then they reached the inn and went in to the warmth, and Martha Hewson saw her husband to bed.","heading":false}]},{"id":"7696831315902964313_63361-h-4.htm","href":"7696831315902964313_63361-h-4.htm.xhtml","linear":true,"types":[],"docTitle":"THE BREAD-WINNER","navLabel":"THE BREAD-WINNER","blocks":[{"text":"THE BREAD-WINNER","heading":true},{"text":"THE BREAD-WINNER","heading":false},{"text":"“Why ain’t ye at work?” repeated his wife.","heading":false},{"text":"He drew his arm away.","heading":false},{"text":"But the humbler Chapel-goer was not daunted.","heading":false},{"text":"The child had come out on to the little terrace.","heading":false},{"text":"And she too stumped down the broken steps.","heading":false},{"text":"“O’ course father were allers fust.”","heading":false},{"text":"And wearily the mother repeated:","heading":false},{"text":"“Yes, father were allers fust.”","heading":false}]},{"id":"7696831315902964313_63361-h-5.htm","href":"7696831315902964313_63361-h-5.htm.xhtml","linear":t